Adequate Directions 21 CFR 801.5
"Adequate directions for use" means directions under which the layman can use a device safely and for the purposes intended.
This includes: Statements of all purposes for which and conditions under which the device can be used; Quantity of dose for each use and usual quantities for persons of different ages and physical conditions; Frequency of administration; Duration of application; Time of administration in relation to other factors; Route or method of application; and Any preparation necessary for use.
